# Bridal Team — environment variables

# ── AI planner ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AI planner works out of the box in "demo mode" (smart, rule-based
# replies). To power it with live Claude AI, add your Anthropic API key.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the model (defaults to claude-sonnet-5)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#
# Optional: total anonymous chat turns allowed per rolling 24h across ALL IPs.
# The backstop behind the 5-a-day per-IP limit, for when IPs are rotated. Left
# unset it defaults to 200/day — roughly $2/day at Sonnet 5 rates. Raise it
# once real signed-out demand justifies the spend. Tripping it is not an
# outage: anonymous callers are asked to sign up, signed-in tiers are
# unaffected.
# AI_ANON_DAILY_GLOBAL_CAP=200

# ── Supabase (venues directory) ───────────────────────────────
# The public Bridal Team project is baked in as a default, so the /vendors
# page reads live venues with no config. Override these to point at your own
# Supabase project instead.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Site / SEO ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical public origin, used for metadataBase, canonical URLs, the sitemap
# and robots.txt. Defaults to https://bridalteam.com. Set this on preview or
# staging deployments so they don't advertise production URLs.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Feature flags ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The /vendors directory is hidden at launch because the `vendors` table
# currently holds seeded sample data (invented names, no websites, no images).
# Set this to true once it holds real listings to bring the page, the nav
# links and the homepage teaser back. Read at build time -- needs a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_VENDOR_DIRECTORY=

# ── Bot protection (Cloudflare Turnstile) ─────────────────────
# Guards signup, login and password reset. Between 11-17 Sep 2026 every signup
# reaching Supabase came from a Tor exit or a datacenter IP -- 49 fake accounts,
# 48 credential-stuffing attempts and 28 password-reset emails sent to harvested
# addresses. This is the control that stops it.
#
# Create a widget at https://dash.cloudflare.com -> Turnstile. You get two keys:
# the SITE key goes here, the SECRET key goes into Supabase.
#
# ⚠️ ORDER MATTERS. Supabase rejects any auth request with no token once its
# captcha setting is on:
#   1. Set this, redeploy. Tokens start flowing; Supabase ignores them.
#   2. THEN turn on Supabase -> Authentication -> Bot and Abuse Protection,
#      choose Turnstile, and paste the SECRET key there.
# Reversing those steps locks every real user out until the deploy catches up.
#
# Left unset, the widget doesn't render and the forms behave as before -- which
# is what makes step 1 safe to ship on its own. Read at build time, so setting
# it needs a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# ── Vendor admin (/admin/venues) ──────────────────────────────
# Both are REQUIRED to add/edit/delete venues from the admin page.
# Find the service-role key in Supabase → Project Settings → API → service_role
# (keep it secret — server-only, never commit it).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Any strong passphrase you choose; you'll type it to unlock /admin/venues.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
